"""ARCH-46 — Obligations & Temporal Intelligence.
One atomic, idempotent apply for the whole milestone (backend, console, verifiers, deploy, docs).

Run from backend/:

    python apply_arch46.py --check      # report every file, write nothing
    python apply_arch46.py              # apply
    python apply_arch46.py              # again: every line reads "already applied"
    python apply_arch46.py --rollback   # restore what the last apply replaced
    python apply_arch46.py --list       # the files this script owns

Accepted starting point: d91421f ("ARCH-45 DONE"). A file already carrying a
later milestone's sentinel (ARCH47-S1: and on) is reported as superseded.
Line endings and a byte-order mark are kept as found (an LF and a CRLF
checkout both apply; the sha256 is taken over LF text).

ARCH46-S1:apply. GENERATED from `git diff d91421f` plus the new files
(32 new, 60 edited through 149 anchors); the generator refuses to
emit if any file carries no ARCH46-S sentinel, and every edit is an anchor that
occurs exactly once when it applies, checked against the final sha256.
"""

